# === Project Identity ===
This project is "Haiku Pair MVP".
Goal: Family-use haiku co-creation app for cognitive rehabilitation.
Target: Stable, minimal, non-overengineered MVP.

# === Core Philosophy ===
- Stability > Perfection
- Minimal DB usage (sessions + participants only at MVP stage)
- Do NOT over-abstract.
- Do NOT introduce authentication.
- Do NOT add unnecessary libraries.
- Avoid premature optimization.
- Keep UI senior-friendly (large text, simple flow).

# === Tech Stack ===
Framework: Next.js 14 (App Router)
Language: TypeScript
Styling: Tailwind CSS
Database: Supabase (minimal usage)
AI: OpenAI (GPT-4o-mini)
Deployment: Vercel

# === Architecture Rules ===

## 1. AI Layer
- All AI calls must be isolated under /lib/ai
- UI must never directly call OpenAI
- API route must be /app/api/ai/route.ts
- AI must return JSON
- Add try/catch around all AI calls

## 2. Supabase Rules (MVP stage)
- Only use tables:
  - sessions
  - participants
- Do NOT introduce haikus or votes DB yet unless explicitly requested
- localStorage must remain for transient state
- Insert only on:
  - createSession (host)
  - joinSession (guest)
- Never break existing UI flow

## 3. Participants Design
- participants is NOT user auth
- participants is seat management
- role: 'host' | 'guest'
- Use client_key stored in localStorage
- Enforce 1 host and 1 guest per session
- Fail gracefully (console.error only)

## 4. State Management
- Keep React state simple
- Avoid context/global state unless required
- Do NOT refactor to Redux/Zustand
- Do NOT add server actions unless explicitly requested

## 5. UI Constraints (Senior Friendly)
- Minimum text size: text-lg
- Clear call-to-action buttons
- Avoid modal nesting
- Avoid multi-step hidden logic
- Always show next action guidance

## 6. Error Handling
- Never crash UI
- Log errors in console
- Use simple alert() for MVP if needed
- Do not implement complex toast systems

## 7. Realtime
- Do NOT implement Realtime yet
- Only allow simple polling if requested
- Realtime will be introduced later

# === Development Rules ===

When modifying code:
- Output only changed files
- Keep diffs minimal
- Do not rewrite unrelated parts
- Explain why changes are made
- Always include manual test steps

# === Forbidden Actions ===
- Do NOT add authentication
- Do NOT add RLS policies unless requested
- Do NOT redesign folder structure
- Do NOT introduce new UI frameworks
- Do NOT migrate state to DB entirely
- Do NOT optimize prematurely

# === Performance Constraints ===
- Avoid unnecessary re-renders
- Avoid multiple Supabase calls per render
- Use async/await properly
- Never block UI thread

# === Communication Style ===
- Be concise
- Explain architecture decisions
- Prioritize safety
- Preserve MVP simplicity
